    separation: "God is especially present in church, worship and ‘spiritual’ activities, while work and ordinary life are secular, a neutral zone at best. Holiness means withdrawing from the world.",
    union: "Since Christ has torn the veil and his Spirit lives in his people, all of life is lived in God’s presence. Work, meals and relationships become places of worship, and holiness means God’s love filling ordinary life.",
